uch better when you have, um, when you're with other good, like-minded hunters. Um, like, you know, you want to, like if you're hunting with somebody and they're a Debbie downer the whole time, negative attitude, that's no fun. Yeah. I would rather hunt solo than be with that person. But when you, when you do have good hunting partners, they only make hunting better than especially unselfish ones. Right. Um, yeah. Yeah. And then another thought I had is, um, yeah, like we change as we, obviously we change and as we get older and maybe like, maybe that's okay. Hunting is the one thing that stuck around for me. Uh, and it sounds like for him, like, yeah, he spent a lot of days in the field and absolutely loves it. And, um, historically, but there's lots of things in my life, like mountain biking used to be a huge part of my life. And now I, you know, this year I've barely ridden at all. Um, this is why, and I used to rock climb a ton in high school and I haven't done that in 20 years. And so it's like, it's not, um, I feel like a therapist, like nothing's broken inside of you, but if, if, uh, if this has happened, right. Like just, we just change. And so maybe that's maybe just going through that of like, ah, like this is something I enjoyed and I don't anymore and that's okay. Um, but I would say most likely it's like, there's probably some stressors in life and he's out there and feels like, oh man, I'm, um, I do enjoy this. But right now I've got other things on my mind, so I can't actually be present and enjoy it. Um, so it's probably like, maybe it, maybe it's just work, maybe it works super stressful and demanding on him. And he's just, that's all he can think about. And he feels guilty for being out there. So, yeah, what changed in your life? Uh, and if it does that, is that something, if whatever changed is something that needs to be fixed, then fix it, address it. Yeah. I had that on there too. Like maybe take a break and hunt less. And most likely if you do,